   "note": "TI SNVSA40B 6.3.3: the TPS61169 keeps a DC path from VIN through L3 and D8 to the LEDs in shutdown, and guarantees OFF only when the array's minimum Vf exceeds the maximum VIN.  This panel is 2.9-3.2 V on a 3.3 V rail, so the screen glows at about 25 mA whenever SW9 is on -- and SW9 is a slide switch, so there is no firmware mitigation.  Q11 breaks the panel cathode return; F5 below is what holds its CONTROL apart from U17's.",
